# --- emulator pipeline -----------------------------------------------------
#
# The tools/ scripts ARE tracked: they are how the emulator is reproduced, and
# tools/training_README.md is the only description of what it does and why.
# What the scripts GENERATE is not tracked, with one deliberate exception.
#
#   ep_make_spectra.py   -> tools/ep_spectra.npz         (836 KB, from CAMB)
#   ep_trainset.slurm    -> runs/                        (11 MB of Monte Carlo)
#   ep_train_final.py    -> tools/ep_emulator.npz        (TRACKED, 8 KB)
#   ep_export_c.py       -> src/model/ep_emu_weights.h   (TRACKED: the artifact)
#   ep_export_test_cases.py -> tests/ep_emu_cases.h      (TRACKED: the fixtures)
#   ep_validate.py       -> tools/ep_validation_mc.npz   (validation ensemble)
#
# ep_emulator.npz is the exception. It is small, and without it the committed
# weights header could only be regenerated by re-running the cluster; with it,
# ep_export_c.py reproduces the header from the repository alone. The header
# records the sha256 of the npz it came from, so the two can be checked against
# each other.

runs/
tools/plots/
tools/ep_spectra.npz
tools/ep_validation_mc.npz
